 {
  "coord": "5:62",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "hedge",
  "note": "The source's two 'if' premises were turned into flat assertions and an 'Is it not so?' was added.",
  "replacement": "Then may we not say, Simmias, that if, as we are always repeating, there is an absolute beauty, and goodness, and an absolute essence of all things; and if we refer all our sensations to this, which is now discovered to have existed in our former state, and compare them with it, finding these ideas to be pre-existent and our inborn possession, then our souls must have had a prior existence; but if not, there would be no force in the argument? The proof that these ideas existed before we were born is the same as the proof that our souls existed before we were born; and if the ideas did not, then neither did the souls."
 },
